{"availability":"available","full":"pcsx-redux/nugget","name":"nugget","description":"Bare-metal libraries and examples for the original PlayStation, including the PSYQo C++ SDK and OpenBIOS.","category":"Developer tools","language":"C","stars":80,"forks":9,"created":"2021-05-29T06:39:22Z","updated":"2026-10-07T01:54:26Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://pcsx-redux.github.io/nugget/","topics":["bare-metal","cpp","homebrew","mips","openbios","playstation","ps1","psx","psyqo","sdk"],"demo":"https://pcsx-redux.github.io/nugget/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:32.045Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:32.045Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:32.045Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:54:32.045Z","stars":80,"forks":9}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Nugget is a collection of bare-metal libraries, runtime pieces, and example projects for the original PlayStation. It is the home of PSYQo, an object-oriented C++ SDK for the console, and of OpenBIOS, a from-scratch reimplementation of Sony's BIOS.","It is built to be consumed as a submodule, so a project can pull in only the parts it needs without dragging along an emulator or a toolchain. PCSX-Redux uses it that way, and its src/mips tree is this repository.","Issues and pull requests are welcome here. To talk about PlayStation development, hacking and reverse engineering, join the PSX.Dev Discord server: []("],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/pcsx-redux/nugget/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"631d0264464d3800874ecc290bc3e54e781640f9fa7e120fbf87972112b5e688","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:32.326Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:32.326Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Nugget is a collection of bare-metal libraries, runtime pieces, and example projects for the original PlayStation. It is the home of PSYQo, an object-oriented C++ SDK for the console, and of OpenBIOS, a from-scratch